      "margin_number": 209,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "A small number of verbs such as βαίνω, ‘I go’ and γιγνώσκω, ‘I get to know’ have a distinct kind of aorist called a ‘root aorist’. The augment and personal endings are added to the absolutely basic aorist stem, or ‘root’, ending in a vowel – in these cases βη/βa- and γνω/γνο-:",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
